# PROJECT: SAMLEY — COMPLETE SAAS APPOINTMENT BOOKING PLATFORM

## 1. YOUR ROLE AND PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, UI/UX designer, database engineer, security engineer and SaaS developer.

Build a complete, production-ready, multi-tenant SaaS appointment-booking platform called **Samley**, a product by **SamTeck Digital**.

Samley is a general-purpose appointment-booking platform for businesses that operate through appointments and scheduled services.

Examples include:
- Salons and barbershops
- Spas and wellness centres
- Beauty and grooming businesses
- Photography studios
- Consultation services
- Other appointment-based businesses

The platform must allow business owners to register their businesses, configure services, receive online bookings, manage appointments, receive payments through Moolre and communicate with customers through SMS.

Customers must be able to access a business's public booking page by scanning its QR code without downloading an application or creating an account.

**Important development instructions:**
- Build a real, functional SaaS platform, not a prototype.
- Do not generate mock, fake, dummy or sample business data.
- Do not create decorative buttons that do nothing.
- Do not introduce features outside the requirements in this document.
- Do not remove or silently change any explicitly requested functionality.
- Do not expose private API keys, service-role keys or payment credentials in frontend code.
- All database operations, payment verification and sensitive business logic must be implemented securely.
- Every major feature must be connected to the actual backend.
- Do not claim that an integration works unless it has been implemented and tested against the provider's actual capabilities.

