The objective is to deliver a real, secure, production-ready Samley SaaS appointment-booking platform.

Do not add unrelated features or make assumptions about business rules that have not been specified.

Where a required external integration depends on provider documentation or merchant approval, verify the actual supported capabilities and clearly identify any unresolved configuration requirement. Do not simulate a successful integration.

Ensure the database schema, backend functions, frontend screens, authentication, payments, notifications and dashboards work together as one coherent application.

The final system must use:
- Samley branding.
- Deep orange and white design.
- Montserrat typography.
- Supabase as the database and backend.
- Moolre for payment processing.
- SMS for transactional notifications.
- PWA functionality.
- Responsive, animated dashboard sidebars.

**Build only the functionality defined in this specification. Do not implement employee or staff management in this release.**